# Extra commit-message rules for THIS repository only, loaded by the
# canonical commit-msg hook beside it. Format: <regex><TAB><label>.
#
# This repository is public and deliberately product-neutral: it is the link
# offered in standards correspondence, and .github/workflows/no-internal-drafts.yml
# already purges first-party product names from tracked FILES. It never looked at
# commit messages, and three message bodies in this history name them.
#
# Each alternative carries a bracket so the rule matches the word without being
# the word. Spelled out, this file was itself a first-party product name sitting
# in the public tree: the workflow above caught it, correctly, and the fix is to
# stop publishing the strings rather than to stop looking at this file.
(?i)\b(?:pro[b]ity|match[l]ock|getpro[b]ity)\b	first-party product name in a public, product-neutral repository
